cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Image Hologram
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-22
authors:
  - family-names: Brisson
    given-names: Jean-François
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374
    affiliation: Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: Mun Seok
license: AGPL-3.0-only
repository-code: https://github.com/sparkainlp-x
abstract: >-
  Pictures stored as interference patterns in a complex
  outer-product holographic memory, reconstructed by projection
  from noisy or fragmented cues. Demonstrates the defining
  holographic property (every fragment contains the whole image)
  and the classification-vs-reconstruction distinction under
  pattern correlation. Stdlib-only Python.
keywords:
  - holographic-memory
  - associative-memory
  - projection
  - image-reconstruction
  - wave-computing
